# Byte-hashed provenance inputs must check out identically on every platform.
#
# `recordDigest()` in lib/stage2b-authored-record.ts hashes this file's RAW BYTES
# (fs.readFileSync with no encoding). That digest is stamped into the generated
# capability-policy.json as `_generatedFrom.record` and asserted by
# scripts/test-stage2b-workbook.ts. On a CRLF checkout the recomputed digest is
# 352cc55022a23d76 instead of the committed da826a3b199357f8, so the assertion
# fails for a reason that has nothing to do with the policy being wrong.
#
# Pinning the input to LF makes that digest checkout-invariant. The fix belongs
# HERE and never in regenerating capability-policy.json: regenerating would bake
# one machine's line endings into a committed artifact and break it for everyone
# whose checkout differs.
#
# Deliberately scoped to the files the inventory found, rather than a repo-wide
# `* text=auto`, which would rewrite 579 index entries for a defect that lives in
# a handful. The inventory is reproducible and asserted by
# scripts/test-checkout-determinism.js.
scripts/fixtures/operation-taxonomy/capability-answers.json text eol=lf

# --- P1.1-R: the SECOND class of checkout-sensitive file ----------------------
#
# The pin above covers a RAW-BYTE hash. It does not cover two other ways a
# tracked text file decides a test result, and both were measured failing at
# 3e3fd55 in a `core.autocrlf=true` checkout while passing under LF:
#
#   (a) BYTE-IDENTITY COMPARISON of a committed generated artifact against what
#       its generator emits right now. The generator writes "\n"; a CRLF checkout
#       puts "\r\n" on disk; the comparison fails with nothing wrong.
#         capability-policy.json     test-stage2b-workbook.ts:569
#         lib/source-health-inventory.ts  test-source-health-inventory.ts:284
#
#   (b) A `readFileSync(path, "utf8")` whose STRING is hashed. Reading as utf8
#       does NOT normalise line endings, so the hash still moves. This one feeds
#       the decision-contract fingerprint, which is stamped into
#       capability-policy.json as `_generatedFrom.contract`, so a CRLF checkout
#       also makes the policy loader refuse a policy that is in fact current.
#         lib/stage2b-plain-language.js   generate-stage2b-workbook.ts:120,130
#
# Measured digests for (b): 7eb6972e3eca8e9c under LF, 5103c29914f31f82 under
# CRLF. The three commands that failed were test-operation-taxonomy,
# test-source-health-inventory and test-stage2b-workbook.
#
# THE FIX IS THE PIN, NEVER REGENERATION. Regenerating any artifact below would
# bake one machine's line endings into a committed file and break the assertion
# for everyone whose checkout differs -- the same trap the pin above records.
scripts/fixtures/operation-taxonomy/capability-policy.json text eol=lf
lib/source-health-inventory.ts text eol=lf
lib/stage2b-plain-language.js text eol=lf

